# The six ex names of the compile mode, each typed on the ex line of an
# editor that has compiled nothing: every name reaches its command, which
# says what it has to say of an editor in that state. What it prints must
# be exactly `expected`.
#
# The echoes name the working directory by its last name, and the gate runs
# the editor in `lean/`, so they read `in lean`. No line holds the
# directory's whole path, and the script starts no process and touches no
# file.

reload
settle

# `next-error` and `previous-error` go to a location of the last
# compilation. Nothing was compiled, so there is none, and each says so.
key : Semicolon shift
commit next-error
key <Enter> Enter -
scene

key : Semicolon shift
commit previous-error
key <Enter> Enter -
scene

# `recompile` runs the last command again, and there is no last command.
key : Semicolon shift
commit recompile
key <Enter> Enter -
scene

# `kill-compilation` stops the compilation that is running, and none is.
key : Semicolon shift
commit kill-compilation
key <Enter> Enter -
scene

# `compile` asks for the command to run, with the prompt `Compile
# command: `, whose scene shows the minibuffer. `<Escape>` cancels it, so
# nothing is started.
key : Semicolon shift
commit compile
key <Enter> Enter -
scene
key <Escape> Escape -

# `compile-command` offers the commands the modes of the working directory
# give. No mode is on there, so it has none to offer.
key : Semicolon shift
commit compile-command
key <Enter> Enter -
scene
